# YOLO Human/Animal Security Detection System

Add a real-time YOLO-based security detector that uses a **dedicated USB camera** (auto-assigned, different from the fish disease camera), streams at stable FPS using the same technique as fish disease, and triggers popup notifications — with a new **AI Security** page in the frontend.

## Proposed Changes

---

### ML Service

#### [NEW] `security_detector.py`
- Reuses the exact same classes from [fish_disease.py](file:///c:/Users/Oshan/Pictures/auqa360/ml-service/fish_disease.py): [ThreadedCamera](file:///c:/Users/Oshan/Pictures/auqa360/ml-service/fish_disease.py#8-73), [DetectionOverlay](file:///c:/Users/Oshan/Pictures/auqa360/ml-service/fish_disease.py#74-173), [StreamCompositor](file:///c:/Users/Oshan/Pictures/auqa360/ml-service/fish_disease.py#174-230)
- Loads **YOLOv8n** (the standard pretrained nano model — detects 80 COCO classes including `person`, [cat](file:///c:/Users/Oshan/Pictures/auqa360/frontend/src/components/NotificationBell.jsx#9-449), `dog`, `bird`, etc.)
- Model file: `ml-service/models/yolov8n.pt` (auto-downloaded by ultralytics on first run)
- Same stable FPS pipeline: threaded camera capture → inference thread → compositor → MJPEG stream
- Detects: `person`, [cat](file:///c:/Users/Oshan/Pictures/auqa360/frontend/src/components/NotificationBell.jsx#9-449), `dog`, `bird`, `horse`, `cow`, `sheep`, `bear`, `elephant`, `zebra`, `giraffe`
- Publishes MQTT: `aquasense/ml/security` with detections, confidence, class names
- MJPEG stream on **port 8766** (separate from fish disease on 8765)

#### [MODIFY] [config.py](file:///c:/Users/Oshan/Pictures/auqa360/ml-service/config.py)
- Add `SECURITY_MODEL_PATH` → `models/yolov8n.pt`
- Add `SECURITY_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD = 0.45`
- Add `TOPIC_SECURITY = "aquasense/ml/security"`
- Add `SECURITY_CAMERA = -1` (auto-assign: pick the first camera NOT used by fish disease)
- Add `SECURITY_STREAM_PORT = 8766`

#### [MODIFY] [main.py](file:///c:/Users/Oshan/Pictures/auqa360/ml-service/main.py)
- Import and instantiate `SecurityDetector`
- Auto camera assignment logic: scan cameras, give fish disease cam index 0, give security next available (e.g. index 1)
- Add `security_loop()` — same structure as [fish_disease_loop()](file:///c:/Users/Oshan/Pictures/auqa360/ml-service/main.py#171-226), publishes to `TOPIC_SECURITY` every frame (throttled to 0.33s MQTT interval)
- Start `security_stream_server` on port 8766
- Add `security` commands to command interface: `security start/stop`, `security camera <index>`
- Publish security model status in [on_mqtt_connect](file:///c:/Users/Oshan/Pictures/auqa360/ml-service/main.py#37-65)
- Subscribe to `aquasense/ml/cmd/security` for start/stop/camera commands

